{
  "devOnly": "mothership:dev-only",
  "version": "board-motion-0.1.0",
  "status": "proposal",
  "about": "Where each character stands in each room on the phone board. A station is a place in the picture, not a seat, a slot or a capacity: the rules impose none (rules/overlays/location-board-layout-v1.json, capacity_note). Which station a character takes depends only on public facts: who is in the room, ordered by seat number. Nothing private, and no arrival order the contract does not carry, chooses a station.",
  "units": "A standing station is [x, row]: x a fraction of the panel's width (three in a row stand at 1/6, 1/2 and 5/6, so that three 44 px targets fit side by side in a 320 px phone's half-width panel), row 0 the front row on the floor, 1 the back row, 2 the far back. Rows are stacked at least one 44 px target apart, and characters in one row at least one target apart, so no two targets overlap. A prop station stands behind a prop lifted from the room's own picture: the character's lower edge sinks behind the prop's edge by the given share of its height. depth scales the drawing (1 = front).",
  "anchor": "Each room picture is pinned so that its anchor line (edge, in the picture's own units) sits at a fixed share of the piece area (at), and scaled to cover the panel: the prop line therefore stays in the same place whatever the panel's size.",
  "rowsFor": "Rows of characters a room needs: none when empty; one for the first two (one, if the room has a prop station); two up to five; three for six to nine. The board gives each band of panels the larger need of its two rooms, and shares what is left of the screen by weight.",
  "weights": {
    "command-room": 0.8,
    "middle": 1.25,
    "lower": 1.0
  },
  "crowd": {
    "about": "Six to nine characters in one room: three rows of three, everyone standing, so that every character is reachable with a 44 px target that overlaps no other. A prop station is not used.",
